WEBVTT

00:00:15.370 --> 00:00:19.620
The police think you're a murderer.

00:00:19.620 --> 00:00:22.830
But I believe in you.

00:00:26.370 --> 00:00:29.450
Ever since he entered Tokyo 7th Prison,

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:33.450
Moriarty mind-controlled various
people he came into contact with,

00:00:33.450 --> 00:00:35.660
forcing them to commit crimes.

00:00:35.660 --> 00:00:37.750
And he put a post-hypnotic
suggestion on them to force them

00:00:37.750 --> 00:00:40.120
to kill themselves when
their crime was found out,

00:00:40.120 --> 00:00:44.120
so that his involvement
would never be uncovered.

00:00:44.120 --> 00:00:46.000
There are three patterns to it.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:47.040
--Hands up, Tetsuo Isshiki!

00:00:47.040 --> 00:00:51.000
--The first, when the police say his name.
--Hands up, Tetsuo Isshiki!

00:00:51.000 --> 00:00:51.910
--Let's end this now. Nao Kaieda.
Umi Sakaguchi. Kiko Takeda.

00:00:51.910 --> 00:00:55.410
--The second, when Moriarty says their name.
--Let's end this now. Nao Kaieda.
Umi Sakaguchi. Kiko Takeda.

00:00:55.410 --> 00:00:57.500
And lastly...

00:00:57.500 --> 00:00:59.160
Where is he?

00:00:59.160 --> 00:01:01.790
What are you talking about?

00:01:01.790 --> 00:01:02.870
Moriarty!

00:01:12.410 --> 00:01:18.200
8020463840.

00:01:18.200 --> 00:01:21.580
When I ask about Moriarty.

00:01:22.790 --> 00:01:24.750
So that's it?

00:01:24.750 --> 00:01:28.120
I was looking into cases where
the criminal killed themselves,

00:01:28.120 --> 00:01:31.660
in other words, incidents where
Moriarty was likely involved.

00:01:31.660 --> 00:01:34.950
And I realized that some of the ones

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:38.830
who committed suicide read
the numbers, and some didn't.

00:01:38.830 --> 00:01:41.830
Oh, like a special stamp.

00:01:41.830 --> 00:01:44.330
I gave it to the ones I liked.

00:01:44.330 --> 00:01:46.330
He tried to throw me off the scent,

00:01:46.330 --> 00:01:49.910
but those numbers were a message.

00:01:49.910 --> 00:01:57.330
I put a four-leaf wood sorrel in this book
and gave it to him when he was in prison.

00:01:57.330 --> 00:02:02.580
But he returned it with a single leaf.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:05.830
When I turned the "4" in the number to a "1,"

00:02:05.830 --> 00:02:08.500
and then put it through
every imaginable permutation,

00:02:08.500 --> 00:02:14.000
I finally found a match
using Japanese pager code.

00:02:15.080 --> 00:02:17.330
"Jame."

00:02:17.330 --> 00:02:19.410
Not "James"?

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:23.830
It's a sign to look at the
last letter of the first names.

00:02:23.830 --> 00:02:27.500
The first names of the killers
who said the numbers.

00:02:27.500 --> 00:02:29.750
And what did you get?

00:02:29.750 --> 00:02:33.040
"Look into the eyes of the PE."

00:02:33.040 --> 00:02:35.370
PE?

00:02:35.370 --> 00:02:39.580
Look into the eyes of the Pink Elephant.

00:02:41.540 --> 00:02:45.500
"See you in Kabukicho!"

00:02:49.290 --> 00:02:53.540
Are the others going to be okay
if they try to lead the police away?

00:02:53.540 --> 00:02:56.950
They'll be fine no matter what happens.

00:02:56.950 --> 00:03:00.620
Look into the eyes of the elephant...

00:03:00.620 --> 00:03:02.660
That building?

00:03:02.660 --> 00:03:06.540
You can't fool me, brother.

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:08.290
Mycroft.

00:03:08.290 --> 00:03:10.330
What are you doing here, brother?

00:03:10.330 --> 00:03:15.250
You don't have the right
to call me brother. I told you that.

00:03:15.250 --> 00:03:17.200
So you won't let me pass, is that it?

00:03:18.250 --> 00:03:20.450
No...

00:03:20.450 --> 00:03:25.620
You're my little brother, and I care about you.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:30.000
Um, he was always cold to you, but...

00:03:30.000 --> 00:03:33.620
He's just a stalker with
a brother obsession, that's all.

00:03:43.830 --> 00:03:46.830
Let me go, brother.

00:03:51.910 --> 00:03:55.370
Don't blame me for whatever happens.

00:03:55.370 --> 00:03:56.700
Thanks.

00:04:08.910 --> 00:04:11.870
He probably lived here.

00:04:11.870 --> 00:04:14.200
In a lonely place like this?

00:04:15.370 --> 00:04:22.120
I heard a lot from Carlyle, the Moran's maid.

00:04:22.120 --> 00:04:27.200
What Moriarty did at that mansion...

00:04:27.200 --> 00:04:32.660
And about Moriarty and his sister, Alexandra...

00:04:37.870 --> 00:04:41.160
Just kill someone one time.

00:04:41.160 --> 00:04:43.580
And if one time isn't enough...

00:04:45.750 --> 00:04:47.790
Kill two people.

00:04:49.200 --> 00:04:51.080
Alexandra...

00:04:55.370 --> 00:04:58.450
What about Alex?

00:04:58.450 --> 00:05:02.160
If she was alive...

00:05:02.160 --> 00:05:05.830
...you wouldn't have ended up like this!

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.700
Here.

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:14.040
Thanks, James...

00:05:15.660 --> 00:05:18.870
Come on, let's go.

00:05:18.870 --> 00:05:21.580
See you later, Alex.

00:05:34.120 --> 00:05:37.040
Carlyle...

00:05:37.040 --> 00:05:41.750
When will the angel come for me?

00:05:41.750 --> 00:05:45.120
I've been such a good girl...

00:05:45.120 --> 00:05:48.540
Why won't he come?

00:05:55.830 --> 00:05:57.330
Water...

00:05:57.330 --> 00:06:00.330
Mom... Carlyle!

00:06:17.200 --> 00:06:19.290
Angel!

00:06:25.290 --> 00:06:27.370
The mistress! The mistress!

00:06:27.370 --> 00:06:28.250
What's wrong?

00:06:28.250 --> 00:06:29.750
What happened?

00:06:32.200 --> 00:06:37.200
Dad's mad. He says I killed mom.

00:06:37.200 --> 00:06:39.290
He doesn't mean it!

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:42.250
He doesn't really think that!

00:06:42.250 --> 00:06:44.910
I made her wonderful, too.

00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:46.540
Wonderful?

00:06:46.540 --> 00:06:51.410
Like a fish in the lake
when lightning strikes...

00:06:55.620 --> 00:06:59.040
Mom was wonderful!

00:07:04.000 --> 00:07:05.790
What's wrong?

00:07:07.080 --> 00:07:11.160
There's a teapot in your heart, James.

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:14.370
And it's got a little hole in it.

00:07:14.370 --> 00:07:17.120
But I'll fix it!

00:07:17.120 --> 00:07:20.540
I'll fill the hole!

00:07:23.250 --> 00:07:28.790
Alexandra, the medicine will kick in
and make you feel better soon.

00:07:28.790 --> 00:07:30.870
It'll be empty...

00:07:32.000 --> 00:07:36.660
Without me, James' teapot will be empty.

00:07:39.500 --> 00:07:42.160
Open the curtains.

00:07:45.040 --> 00:07:48.200
My only reason for living is James.

00:07:49.580 --> 00:07:52.160
I have to do my best...

00:07:52.160 --> 00:07:56.830
James is keeping me alive!

00:07:56.830 --> 00:08:03.040
Alexandra knew about you!

00:08:03.040 --> 00:08:07.250
And yet she still tried to stop you!

00:08:07.250 --> 00:08:13.500
And at some point, that became
all that was keeping her alive...

00:08:14.910 --> 00:08:18.700
I kept Alex alive?

00:08:20.500 --> 00:08:26.500
She said that Moriarty left,
looking like he was about to cry.

00:08:30.330 --> 00:08:32.080
This is the room.

00:08:38.250 --> 00:08:39.830
"Morairty's Hideout"

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:43.080
"Morairty's Hideout"

00:08:39.830 --> 00:08:43.080
So this is Morairty's...

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:53.790
It's locked!

00:08:53.790 --> 00:08:56.290
You're late.

00:08:56.290 --> 00:08:57.620
Moriarty!

00:08:57.620 --> 00:08:59.540
Is that you?

00:08:59.540 --> 00:09:01.830
Hey, can you see me?

00:09:01.830 --> 00:09:03.950
Over here!

00:09:09.950 --> 00:09:13.580
You're alive...

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:16.870
Now, a normal reunion would be boring.

00:09:16.870 --> 00:09:18.200
So let's play a game!

00:09:18.200 --> 00:09:19.410
A game?

00:09:19.410 --> 00:09:24.660
You're locked in a room with a bomb.

00:09:24.660 --> 00:09:29.700
If you can't get to me in the
far back room within ten minutes...

00:09:29.700 --> 00:09:30.910
Boom!

00:09:33.000 --> 00:09:34.700
Bye, see you later!

00:09:34.700 --> 00:09:36.660
Wait, Moriarty!

00:09:38.950 --> 00:09:40.370
What's this?

00:09:40.370 --> 00:09:43.750
You give it to him, right?

00:09:48.410 --> 00:09:49.620
What is that?

00:09:49.620 --> 00:09:51.120
Bliking?

00:09:51.120 --> 00:09:52.620
A code.

00:09:52.620 --> 00:09:54.500
Four digits.

00:09:54.500 --> 00:09:56.290
The number of fans?

00:09:56.290 --> 00:09:58.290
But that changes.

00:09:58.290 --> 00:10:02.080
The head of a Bliking is the tastiest part.

00:10:02.080 --> 00:10:05.700
But what number is the butt, in terms of riches?

00:10:05.700 --> 00:10:08.540
Think about it...

00:10:08.540 --> 00:10:10.830
The head is the tastiest part,

00:10:10.830 --> 00:10:14.080
but what number is the butt, in terms of riches?

00:10:14.080 --> 00:10:18.910
Bliking... Bliking... Bliking...

00:10:18.910 --> 00:10:22.870
Oh, <i>buri</i> ! <i>Buri</i> is a delicious fish!
[ <i>Buri</i> : Amberjack]

00:10:22.870 --> 00:10:25.450
But that's got nothing to do with numbers, huh?

00:10:25.450 --> 00:10:26.870
Twelfth.

00:10:26.870 --> 00:10:27.790
"Fisherman"

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:32.410
"Fisherman"

00:10:27.790 --> 00:10:32.410
<i>Buri</i> caught in December is the tastiest.

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:34.160
"Fisherman"

00:10:32.410 --> 00:10:34.160
The 12th month.

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:36.290
The "head" is 12, for the <i>buri</i> .

00:10:36.290 --> 00:10:38.830
But what is the "king" on the butt?

00:10:38.830 --> 00:10:40.370
In terms of riches.

00:10:40.370 --> 00:10:43.500
In other words, in a game
of Japanese millionaire, the king

00:10:43.500 --> 00:10:48.830
is the fourth strongest card after
the Joker, the two, and the ace.

00:10:48.830 --> 00:10:50.790
So four.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:54.500
The answer is 1204.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:13.040
We have to find another four-digit code!

00:11:14.700 --> 00:11:15.540
Open it up.

00:11:15.540 --> 00:11:16.370
Me?

00:11:16.370 --> 00:11:18.080
Now.

00:11:31.660 --> 00:11:34.160
Oh, it's a toy.

00:11:34.500 --> 00:11:37.450
"Height ?cm"
"Month"        "Day"

00:11:38.370 --> 00:11:41.700
I don't know what it means...

00:11:41.700 --> 00:11:43.500
It's a bad joke.

00:11:43.500 --> 00:11:44.790
A joke?

00:11:44.790 --> 00:11:47.290
That's the "shortstop" position on the field:

00:11:47.290 --> 00:11:48.700
" <i>yuugeki</i> ."

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:52.870
"Taichou"

00:11:48.700 --> 00:11:52.870
And this is the height of a body.
" <i>Taichou</i> " in Japanese.

00:11:52.870 --> 00:11:55.290
<i>Yuugeki Taichou</i> ?
[Captain of the Irregulars]

00:11:55.290 --> 00:11:56.790
Moriarty.

00:11:56.790 --> 00:11:58.450
And one is...

00:12:01.120 --> 00:12:03.870
So two and three are...

00:12:11.290 --> 00:12:14.200
Moriarty's birthday is June 2nd.

00:12:14.200 --> 00:12:15.830
0602.

00:12:15.830 --> 00:12:18.370
My birthday is August 7th.

00:12:18.370 --> 00:12:21.160
January 6th for me.

00:12:21.160 --> 00:12:26.410
Add them all together and you get...

00:12:26.410 --> 00:12:28.500
1515.

00:12:33.870 --> 00:12:35.370
Again?

00:12:38.870 --> 00:12:41.040
That's in bad taste.

00:12:43.580 --> 00:12:46.200
There's a key we need this time.

00:12:50.250 --> 00:12:51.620
Right, right.

00:12:51.620 --> 00:12:53.950
You want me to open it, right?

00:13:01.540 --> 00:13:05.000
"The gentle one turns its back before the Missus,

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:07.330
Attach the two pairs of rats.

00:13:07.330 --> 00:13:09.790
The door will open."

00:13:09.790 --> 00:13:11.540
Rats?

00:13:15.910 --> 00:13:17.870
There's only one.

00:13:17.870 --> 00:13:20.200
This is the other.

00:13:20.200 --> 00:13:22.160
"Gentle"

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:29.120
Um, the gentle one turns its back, so...

00:13:29.120 --> 00:13:31.580
Okay, that's the first pair.

00:13:31.580 --> 00:13:35.080
Find the other and you can
come into the room with me.

00:13:35.080 --> 00:13:37.000
You've got one minute left!

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:40.200
But there are no more rats!

00:13:40.200 --> 00:13:44.790
Hint! Don't be embarrassed!

00:13:44.790 --> 00:13:46.080
Embarrassed?

00:13:46.080 --> 00:13:48.790
Hell no! I'm not doing that!

00:13:48.790 --> 00:13:50.450
You solved it?

00:13:50.450 --> 00:13:53.160
If you solved it then bring the rats.

00:13:53.160 --> 00:13:54.500
They're already here.

00:13:54.500 --> 00:13:56.870
They are?

00:13:58.040 --> 00:14:01.000
Mouse... and Mouth?

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:02.950
Ten seconds?

00:14:02.950 --> 00:14:05.040
We have to do it!

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:07.000
I'm the kind one so...

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:09.330
You stand here, Sherlock!

00:14:17.160 --> 00:14:18.540
That's the right answer.

00:14:18.540 --> 00:14:21.950
Congrats. The bomb is disarmed.

00:14:34.660 --> 00:14:36.120
"Moriarty the Living"

00:14:38.040 --> 00:14:39.580
What's this?

00:14:40.620 --> 00:14:44.500
Now tell me, Sherlock.

00:14:44.500 --> 00:14:49.540
What am I? What is Moriarty?

00:15:18.830 --> 00:15:21.000
You not here, old man?

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:24.870
Come on, old man, get your butt out here!

00:15:31.330 --> 00:15:33.580
Knock it off.

00:15:33.580 --> 00:15:36.790
Sherlock.

00:15:36.790 --> 00:15:38.540
Old man!

00:15:38.540 --> 00:15:42.330
You vanished, so I got worried!

00:15:42.330 --> 00:15:44.200
Where were you going on?

00:15:44.200 --> 00:15:47.830
I got sick so I went to the baths.

00:15:47.830 --> 00:15:49.790
So, what do you want?

00:15:49.790 --> 00:15:55.290
Remember that guy named Moriarty
who fell off a building a month ago?

00:15:55.290 --> 00:15:57.750
Who was that guy?

00:15:57.750 --> 00:16:02.290
Was he just a murderer?

00:16:02.290 --> 00:16:04.910
I don't know...

00:16:04.910 --> 00:16:07.830
Well, that doesn't help.

00:16:07.830 --> 00:16:12.830
If somebody had been able to
help Moriarty after Alex's death...

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:15.620
Maybe he could've been a normal person.

00:16:15.620 --> 00:16:18.660
But Alex was his twin, right?

00:16:18.660 --> 00:16:22.660
Could anybody have taken her place?

00:16:22.660 --> 00:16:26.500
Maybe the guy named "Sherlock" could have.

00:16:26.500 --> 00:16:30.250
The pervert who stayed with him till the end?

00:16:30.250 --> 00:16:33.580
But he's no different than Moriarty, is he?

00:16:33.580 --> 00:16:37.660
I can't see him taking Alex's place.

00:16:37.660 --> 00:16:42.830
He couldn't have sealed up the hole
in his heart, like Alex could have.

00:16:42.830 --> 00:16:44.120
But you see...

00:16:44.120 --> 00:16:47.700
He could've showed him
how he sealed up his own hole.

00:16:47.700 --> 00:16:51.120
Why he didn't become a murderer.

00:16:51.120 --> 00:16:56.870
Maybe that would've made
him into a normal person.

00:16:56.870 --> 00:17:00.370
So why didn't he?

00:17:00.370 --> 00:17:03.950
Because he couldn't, even if he wanted to.

00:17:03.950 --> 00:17:06.410
He had a brother named Mycroft.

00:17:06.410 --> 00:17:09.410
He encountered <i>rakugo</i> in Kabukicho.

00:17:09.410 --> 00:17:14.500
He learned about mystery-solving
<i>rakugo</i> from Moriarty.

00:17:14.500 --> 00:17:18.580
And he met Watson.

00:17:18.580 --> 00:17:21.120
Sherlock was lucky. That's all.

00:17:21.120 --> 00:17:28.080
He didn't know anything
about himself. Or Moriarty.

00:17:28.080 --> 00:17:32.080
So the reason Moriarty became a murder was...

00:17:32.080 --> 00:17:34.540
He was unlucky?

00:17:34.540 --> 00:17:36.950
You can call it "luck" if you like.

00:17:36.950 --> 00:17:39.370
But if he had more time,

00:17:39.370 --> 00:17:41.580
he would've experienced good luck, bad luck,

00:17:41.580 --> 00:17:44.080
fun things, painful things, so many things...

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:50.290
And from then, he would've learned
how to get along with this world.

00:17:50.290 --> 00:17:53.410
Like Sherlock did.

00:17:53.410 --> 00:18:01.450
But when he killed Jack, that became impossible.

00:18:01.450 --> 00:18:03.200
But after he became a murderer,

00:18:03.200 --> 00:18:05.830
he still wanted to be friends
with Sherlock, right?

00:18:05.830 --> 00:18:11.290
He can't kill anybody without a friend?
What a lame murderer...

00:18:11.290 --> 00:18:13.450
Shut your mouth, fool!

00:18:13.450 --> 00:18:18.620
Why are you so mad?

00:18:18.620 --> 00:18:23.040
Even so, he wanted to be with others...

00:18:23.040 --> 00:18:30.250
A good man or a bad man... He was still a man.

00:18:30.250 --> 00:18:35.120
Moriarty was a man like any other.

00:18:35.120 --> 00:18:38.370
And a mere child of 16!

00:18:40.790 --> 00:18:43.000
Stop...

00:18:43.000 --> 00:18:45.250
He was lonely and sad,

00:18:45.250 --> 00:18:48.290
and he wanted someone to understand.

00:18:48.290 --> 00:18:50.950
There's nothing strange about that at all.

00:18:53.500 --> 00:18:59.700
Moriarty, if only I'd... if only
I'd been there for you more...

00:18:59.700 --> 00:19:06.750
If I'd been there to hold you,
we could've made it work, I think...

00:19:08.290 --> 00:19:10.410
I'm sorry.

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:22.910
How is Moriarty beyond the
mirror like a one night stand?

00:19:22.910 --> 00:19:24.620
I don't know, how?

00:19:24.620 --> 00:19:28.330
With both of them,

00:19:28.330 --> 00:19:30.660
when you shoot, it's goodbye.

00:19:51.950 --> 00:19:56.500
I knew you wouldn't be coming with me.

00:19:56.500 --> 00:20:01.250
When Alex told me to keep loving this world...

00:20:01.250 --> 00:20:04.950
But that's not what Alex meant!

00:20:04.950 --> 00:20:07.660
That was because she thought
that if I didn't love this world,

00:20:07.660 --> 00:20:13.950
there'd be no reason for her to live.

00:20:13.950 --> 00:20:17.160
I was surprised when Carlyle told me that.

00:20:17.160 --> 00:20:21.910
To think, a person like me,
keeping someone alive!

00:20:21.910 --> 00:20:24.750
And then I thought...

00:20:26.700 --> 00:20:30.540
If Alex was alive...

00:20:30.540 --> 00:20:34.540
Maybe that world would've been possible.

00:20:39.950 --> 00:20:47.080
At the time I didn't know why
I went to get back Alex's hairpin.

00:20:47.080 --> 00:20:52.370
But I realized that it might be
because I wanted to watch the world,

00:20:52.370 --> 00:20:54.540
the world that you're all in.

00:20:54.540 --> 00:20:58.290
So I decided to leave this letter.

00:21:03.540 --> 00:21:08.370
All the craziness in the row house
was actually pretty fun.

00:21:08.370 --> 00:21:12.080
Watson came, you changed...

00:21:12.080 --> 00:21:18.660
It was strange, but at the same time,
it was still wonderful.

00:21:18.660 --> 00:21:26.870
You began to face your heart and love
this world. I was so jealous of you.

00:21:26.870 --> 00:21:30.580
I wished I was so lucky.

00:21:30.580 --> 00:21:34.000
I wanted to be like you.

00:21:34.000 --> 00:21:36.160
I'm glad I met you.

00:21:36.160 --> 00:21:39.160
Farewell, Sherlock Holmes.

00:21:40.330 --> 00:21:45.160
Gotcha, dummy!

00:21:49.580 --> 00:21:50.040
"Shinjuku Ward"

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:52.370
"Shinjuku Ward"

00:21:50.040 --> 00:21:52.370
Shinjuku's west side.

00:21:52.370 --> 00:21:57.410
On the other side of the wall from
its well-ordered, well-lit streets

00:21:57.410 --> 00:21:59.660
lies the chaos of the east.

00:22:01.160 --> 00:22:03.620
In the darkness of Kabukicho,

00:22:03.620 --> 00:22:05.290
where elephants roar to sound the time,

00:22:05.290 --> 00:22:07.500
and villains lurk in every shadow,

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:10.620
you'll find seven detectives.

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:11.830
"Sherlock Holmes" "John H Watson"

00:22:10.620 --> 00:22:11.830
Weirdos, freaks, bozos and fools to a man,

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:12.830
"Kyogoku Fuyuto"

00:22:11.830 --> 00:22:12.830
Weirdos, freaks, bozos and fools to a man,

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:13.830
"Michel Belmont"

00:22:12.830 --> 00:22:13.830
who knows what madness they'll bring with them.

00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:14.790
"Lucy Morstan" "Mary Morstan"

00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:14.790
who knows what madness they'll bring with them.

00:22:14.790 --> 00:22:15.500
"Kobayashi Torataro"

00:22:15.500 --> 00:22:20.330
Enjoy this the mystery-solving
battle of the detectives.

00:22:28.700 --> 00:22:31.870
You're sure it's him, Captain?

00:22:31.870 --> 00:22:34.660
No doubt at all, from the MO.

00:22:34.660 --> 00:22:38.950
But why did you come to us?

00:22:38.950 --> 00:22:40.700
Righteous anger!

00:22:40.700 --> 00:22:44.750
I don't want to see any more victims!

00:22:44.750 --> 00:22:46.660
That's what you always say.

00:22:46.660 --> 00:22:49.500
You're planning on taking
the credit for yourself, right?

00:22:49.500 --> 00:22:53.370
Not that I care, as long as I get paid!

00:22:55.080 --> 00:22:57.950
When the sun sets in other towns,

00:22:57.950 --> 00:23:01.000
in our town the neon lights turn on.

00:23:01.000 --> 00:23:03.870
If you want gold and silver...

00:23:03.870 --> 00:23:07.040
Solve the mystery before the others...

00:23:07.040 --> 00:23:09.910
This row house is filled
with the strangest of men.

00:23:09.910 --> 00:23:14.290
People call it "The Detective's Row House."

00:23:15.410 --> 00:23:17.040
A whistle at midnight.

00:23:17.040 --> 00:23:18.370
Cigar smoke.

00:23:18.370 --> 00:23:23.790
Dr. Grimesby Roylott is one
of Shinjuku's finest doctors.

00:23:23.790 --> 00:23:25.830
This'll be rough, Sherlock.

00:23:25.830 --> 00:23:27.750
It'll be easy.

00:23:27.750 --> 00:23:30.790
For us, anyway.

00:23:30.790 --> 00:23:32.160
What did you say?

00:23:32.160 --> 00:23:34.500
Quiet!

00:23:34.500 --> 00:23:38.950
Ten million yen for the one who solves
the mystery of House Roylott!

00:23:38.950 --> 00:23:40.330
Ready...

00:23:40.330 --> 00:23:41.620
Go!
